00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.020
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:06.870
That number is two one nine two David P here
is a question that I'm gonna assume is being

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.870
asked in good faith, but it hasn't been answered
so many times.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.080
Take a listen.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.630
My name is Louis G. would you kindly address
the tax increase?

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:28.710
That would probably happen if Sanders or Warren
instituted their Medicare for all bill probably

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.160
worded that incorrectly, but you know what
I mean.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.160
Yeah.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.320
Listen, so Elizabeth Warren doesn't have a
Medicare for all bill.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.160
She said she likes Bernie's, but she's open
to other ideas.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.760
We don't know exactly how her plan would be
funded.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.860
Although she has said total costs would go
down, the rich and corporations would pay

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.860
more.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.520
Okay, let's focus on Bernie's.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.380
Bernie has addressed the costs and I've addressed
the costs.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.030
Your total costs would go down under Medicare
for all.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.060
There would be a payroll tax that is added.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.220
It would be a couple percentage points to
the average worker.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.559
Corporations would pay a piece of it as well.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:07.619
Premiums go away, copays go away, co-insurance
goes away.

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:12.520
All of these costs go down and then you pay
a little bit through your payroll tax.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.200
If you can't afford it, if you don't have
a job, that's okay.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.119
The numbers account for that already this
has been addressed.

00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:25.090
There is a fair criticism that Bernie is not
always the most, uh, solid in terms of his

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.509
messaging of how this will work.

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:28.689
It's been addressed.

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:33.900
The proposal to pay for it is out there, and
I'm not criticizing the collar, but lots of

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:40.091
people just haven't seen that to continue
to pretend as some are doing, that the cost

00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:45.529
element hasn't been addressed or that the
tax element hasn't been dealt with.

00:01:45.529 --> 00:01:46.529
It has now.

00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:47.759
You might not like it.

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:49.420
You might disagree with the approach.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.009
You could disagree that the numbers have been
calculated correctly.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:55.590
Reasonable people can disagree about whether
the cost of the program has been properly

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.590
assessed.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.610
That's all very reasonable.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:03.789
